A||||5||Homicidal||Air still in the clutch? MORE bleeding??!? ||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||04-25-2000||08:23 PM||||I bled the clutch, but my pedal still feels light and not much spring or pressure to it. I can start the car in neutral with the pedal depressed but not in any gears. It just lurches foward some and then dies.<BR>Do I still have air in the system or is my problem more than just air?? <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||04-25-2000||08:36 PM||||I'm sure we will get all sorts of different answers here, but I would continue with the air in the line theory.<P>Heres a trick I have found sucessful every time. It is called gravity bleeding for obvious reasons. First take the cap off the master cylinder and fill the resivoir to the top. Then open up the bleeder valve on the slave(open it up a ways). Fluid should start to makes it's way through the bleeder valve) I always put a wrag under the slave to catch all the fluid. Just keep the master full. Usually takes 10 minutes to get a perfect pedal feel. No need to even raise the front of the vehicle, I actually find it doesn't work as well with the front end raised. Hope this helps, it is a very easy way to bleed the system.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Princess46||04-25-2000||10:56 PM||||I'm going to agree with the air in the line!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||04-26-2000||05:28 AM||||Check the clutch shaft lever travel, it should move nearly an inch when the pedal is depressed.  If it does then your problem is a more likely being caused by a cracked lever.  They tend to crack where they clamp to the shaft, and the resulting slippage causes clutch disengagement failure.<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Homicidal||04-26-2000||09:58 AM||||Would it feel like a "soft pedal"?||||reg||1
Z||000005||mwbackus||04-27-2000||12:51 AM||||A cracked clutch release lever will feel like a soft pedal.  But, you dont have to take my advise, as I have only been working on these things for 12 yrs.  I am sure they will fix the lever when they install the new clutch you really didnt need anyway..<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
